{"name":"Blue Aura","hex":"#6c7386","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"aura","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A subtle emanation or exhalation of any substance, such as an aroma or odour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A distinctive atmosphere or quality surrounding or associated with something or someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aura"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aura (paranormal)","blocks":[{"text":"In parapsychology and some spiritual traditions, an aura, or energy field, is said to be an emanation produced by and surrounding the body of a person, animal or object, unique to the individual, and which is typically regarded to be an ever present and essential part of its being. In some esoteric positions, the aura is described as a subtle body. Psychics and holistic medicine practitioners often claim to have the ability to see the size, color and type of vibration of an aura."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Aura_diagram.png/330px-Aura_diagram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aura_(paranormal)","wikidata":"Q1154226"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg/250px-Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg/250px-Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charles Webster Leadbeater is credited with developing and popularizing the concept of auras.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Lotus_Kirlian.jpg/330px-Lotus_Kirlian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Lotus_Kirlian.jpg/330px-Lotus_Kirlian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artistic representation of a man in the Lotus position, surrounded by a blue glow","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALotus_Kirlian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baraducforcevital.tif/lossle